{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ומדותם מחוץ לעיר וגו' אלפים באמה", :translit "u-madotem mi-chutz la-ir vegomer alpayim ba-amah", :gloss "and you shall measure from outside the city etc. two thousand cubits"} {:he "אלפים אמה", :translit "alpayim amah", :gloss "two thousand cubits"} {:he "שבעים אמה", :translit "shiv'im amah", :gloss "seventy cubits"} {:he "שיריים", :translit "shirayim", :gloss "remainder"} {:he "ומדותם מחוץ לעיר", :translit "u-madotem mi-chutz la-ir", :gloss "and you shall measure from outside the city"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Interprets 'two thousand cubits' as measured beyond the city's 70-cubit width plus remainder, not inclusive of it."}], :frame {:text "The verse states the Levite cities' pastureland extends 'two thousand cubits' from the city wall. The opening word of the verse, ומדותם (Erashei HaTzibbur edition: וְהִתְנַחֲלִתֶּם), is read as 'and you shall measure' (from מדה), so 'two thousand cubits from outside the city' means the full 2000-amah perimeter is measured beyond the city's own dimensions. Ba'al HaTurim cites that the city's width is reckoned as 70 cubits plus a remainder, citing the Talmudic discussion of Levite city measurements in tractate Eruvin.", :sources ["Eruvin 55a-b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Interprets 'two thousand cubits' as measured beyond the city's 70-cubit width plus remainder, not inclusive of it.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:32:54.104925959Z", :model "glm-5.2"}